  "body": "## What happens\n\nWhen an operation's Geometry has a picked face, the viewport draws the face outline as a thick violet stroke with a dark halo (`pick_ink` -> `pick_highlight_mesh::paint_selected`, #1505). Seen from a low angle, the stroke becomes a wedge: a second violet line separates from the outline and grows wider toward the edge of the viewport, until it reaches the edge.\n\n- The wedge shows in all themes (dark and light).\n- The line width and the anti-aliasing do not change it. It shows at 1 pt with anti-aliasing Off on the #2958 branch.\n\n<img width=\"520\" height=\"315\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b3610788-dfea-41b9-a7c6-726d731a385a\" />\n\n<img width=\"521\" height=\"328\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8a07c9a4-7520-4994-bbc5-92cbfc675652\" />\n\n## Where it comes from\n\nThese three builds were compared at the same low view of the same project (a picked top face, Face operation):\n\n| Build | Result |\n|---|---|\n| v0.24.0 release | No wedge. Some halo segments disappear at some angles and zoom levels (see below). |\n| `main` at acd5b02d3 | Wedge |\n| `main` + #2989 | Wedge |\n\nThe pick highlight was rewritten after v0.24.0, in PR #2256 (#2201: cached geometry, one batched mesh of stroke paths). Thus the wedge is a regression of that change.\n\n- A probe of `egui::epaint::Tessellator` with a thin, acute closed path does not extend past its points. Thus a miter at a sharp corner is probably not the cause.\n- A likely cause is the screen projection of the world points. `push_screen_polyline_runs` projects each point by itself (`interact::project_uv`).\n  - A point behind the eye (`w <= 1e-6`) is dropped, and the run continues to the next point that projects.\n  - A point just in front of the near plane projects to a very large screen position.\n  - Neither case clips the segment at the near plane, so a run can connect two points that are not neighbours on the outline, or go to a point far off the screen.\n\n## Related: the halo that disappears (also in v0.24.0)\n\nIn v0.24.0, at some angles and zoom levels, parts of the thick stroke disappear, and only the thin depth-tested overlay line stays. The cause is the same projection: a segment with an end behind the eye is dropped. This is older than the wedge.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe thick pick outline follows the picked edges at each angle and zoom. A segment that crosses the near plane is clipped at the near plane. It is not dropped, and it is not connected to another part of the outline.\n\n## Done means\n\n- Each segment of the selected-pick and hover highlights is clipped at the near plane in clip space before it is projected.\n- A run never joins two points that are not neighbours on the outline.\n- A test with a picked rectangle seen from a low angle, with a corner behind the eye:\n  - Each stroke vertex stays within the stroke width of the projected (clipped) outline.\n  - No segment of the outline is missing.\n\nFound during the test of #2958 (PR #2989). #2989 does not change this code.\n\nProposed labels: `bug`, `P3`, `effort:medium`, `area:ui`, `source:agent`\n",
